  "riskClass": "medium",
  "title": "SuppliersPage search debounce effect has fetchSuppliers in useEffect but not in dependency array",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: Wiring. Severity: P2. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. The debounced search useEffect (line 305-331) depends on [searchTerm] but calls fetchSuppliers which is a useCallback that depends on [accessToken]. The eslint-disable comment on line 331 suppresses the missing dependency warning. If accessToken changes (e.g., after a token refresh), the search effect won't re-fire with the new token, potentially causing 401 errors on the next search. Additionally, line 312-315 checks `if (searchTerm === '')` and then conditionally refetches `if (suppliers.length > 0 || error)`, but on initial mount searchTerm is '' AND suppliers.length is 0 AND error is '', so it skips the refetch - this is correct but fragile.",
